-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07: worked households.
--
-- EVERY EXPECTED VALUE COMES FROM THE SOURCE AND THE ROWS' SOURCED FIGURES,
-- worked by hand in NOTES.md section 5 (and checked there with exact
-- fractions), never from running this code. The figures:
--   credit point 2026 ....... NIS 2,904 a year (ITA 2025 value, IL-01; fixed for
--                             2026 by ITO s 120B(e)(1), IL-03)
--   s 121 brackets 2026 ..... 10% to 84,120; 14% to 120,720; 20% to 228,000;
--                             31% to 301,200; 35% to 560,280; 47% above
--                             (source lines 4351-4358; enacted by the Economic
--                             Efficiency Law 5786-2026 s 5, from 1 January 2026)
--   s 121B(a) 2026 .......... 3% above 721,560 ([booklet-2026] PDF p. 8)
--   personal points ......... 2 (s 34) + 1/4 (s 36), + 1/2 for a woman (s 36A)
--   children's points ....... s 66(c)(4) for the woman, (5) for the man
--   NII threshold 2026 ...... 7,703 (IL-04, IL-05: the Institute)
--   column D 2026 ........... 1.04% up to it, 4.67% above (IL-04, the items)
--                             -- READ AT THE PRINTED TOTALS from Meng's ruling of
--                             2026-10-07: 1.04% up to it, 7.00% above (source
--                             line 4730; the Institute deducts 7%). The items'
--                             reading is kept as a fork (NOTES.md K14).
--   Schedule K 2026 ......... maximum 51,910 a month; minimum the minimum wage,
--                             6,247.67 (Jan-Mar), 6,443.85 (Apr-Dec) (IL-05)
--   child allowance 2026 .... 173 first and fifth on, 219 second to fourth (IL-06)
--   health (an INPUT) ....... the caller's figure; here 3.23% up to 7,703 and
--                             5.17% above, on the salary up to 51,910 - the
--                             Institute's published employee health rates
--                             (IL-04 NOTES.md section 7), applied by the test
--                             author, not by any rule.
-- A failing assertion is a finding: no expected value here is ever edited to
-- match what the code computed.
--
-- VERSION 0.2.0 (2026-10-07). Eleven expected values below changed because row
-- IL-08 now encodes a provision this module's households reach; each carries a
-- "CHANGED IN 0.2.0" comment citing the provision, and NOTES.md section 11 lists
-- them with their old values. None changed to match a run: each was worked by
-- hand (NOTES.md section 11) before the module was run against version 0.2.0.
-- MENG'S RULING OF 2026-10-07 (Schedule J column D at the printed totals by
-- default) changed twenty more, each marked "CHANGED BY THE SCHEDULE J RULING"
-- with the figure it replaced; NOTES.md section 11.13 lists them.
-- The households of version 0.2.0's new paths are in il07-tests-il08.l4.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 — worked households`

§§ `Builders`

-- An ordinary resident employee, paid the same salary in every month of 2026.
-- A woman's age under Schedule A1 Part D: 70 years (840 months) for a woman born
-- in May 1950 or later (source line 4453, as row IL-05 reads it).
GIVEN `the earner's given name` IS A STRING
      `is female`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `born on`                 IS A DATE
      `salary`                  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `IL-07 earner`
`test: an earner` `the earner's given name` `, female:` `is female` `, born` `born on` `, paid` `salary` MEANS
    `IL-07 earner` WITH
        `the earner's name`                                                              IS `the earner's given name`
        `the earner is a woman`                                                          IS `is female`
        `the earner's date of birth`                                                     IS `born on`
        `the earner's monthly salary`                                                    IS `salary`
        `the earner is paid that salary in every month of the tax year`                  IS TRUE
        `the earner was an Israeli resident in the tax year, under the Income Tax Ordinance` IS TRUE
        `the earner is a foreign worker`                                                 IS FALSE
        `the earner is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`             IS FALSE
        `the earner is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS TRUE
        `the earner is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS TRUE
        `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over applies to the earner` IS TRUE
        `the earner's age fixed by Part D of Schedule A1 to the National Insurance Law, in months, if a woman` IS
            IF `is female` THEN JUST 840 ELSE NOTHING
        `the earner has no credit or deduction under the Income Tax Ordinance beyond those the composed rows encode` IS TRUE

-- A wife who does not work, married to an insured man: a "housewife" under NII
-- s 238 (source line 2428), so not insured under Chapter 11.
GIVEN `her name` IS A STRING
GIVETH AN `IL-07 spouse`
`test: a housewife named` `her name` MEANS
    `IL-07 spouse` WITH
        `the spouse's name`                                                              IS `her name`
        `the spouse is a woman`                                                          IS TRUE
        `the spouse's taxable income in the tax year`                                    IS 0
        `the spouse is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS FALSE
        `the spouse is a housewife as defined in section 238 of the National Insurance Law` IS TRUE
        `the spouse is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS TRUE

-- A husband who does not work: insured under Chapter 11; never a "housewife".
GIVEN `his name` IS A STRING
GIVETH AN `IL-07 spouse`
`test: a husband at home named` `his name` MEANS
    `IL-07 spouse` WITH
        `the spouse's name`                                                              IS `his name`
        `the spouse is a woman`                                                          IS FALSE
        `the spouse's taxable income in the tax year`                                    IS 0
        `the spouse is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`           IS TRUE
        `the spouse is a housewife as defined in section 238 of the National Insurance Law` IS FALSE
        `the spouse is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`             IS TRUE

GIVEN `the other spouse`  IS AN `IL-07 spouse`
      `registered`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `claims`            IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `IL-07 couple`
`test: married to` `the other spouse` `, the earner registered:` `registered` `, the earner claims a separate calculation:` `claims` MEANS
    `IL-07 couple` WITH
        `the earner's spouse`                                                            IS `the other spouse`
        `the earner is the registered spouse`                                            IS `registered`
        `the earner claims a separate calculation of the tax on the earner's income from personal exertion` IS `claims`
        `the earner would be entitled to a credit point under section 37 of the Income Tax Ordinance` IS FALSE

GIVEN `the child's given name` IS A STRING
      `born on`                IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `IL-07 child`
`test: a child` `the child's given name` `, born` `born on` MEANS
    `IL-07 child` WITH
        `the child's name`                                                               IS `the child's given name`
        `the child's date of birth`                                                      IS `born on`
        `the child's mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS FALSE

GIVEN `the year`    IS A NUMBER
      `the month`   IS A NUMBER
      `who earns`   IS AN `IL-07 earner`
      `the couple`  IS A MAYBE `IL-07 couple`
      `the kids`    IS A LIST OF `IL-07 child`
      `health`      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `IL-07 household in a month`
`test: in` `the year` `month` `the month` `, a household of` `who earns` `, married:` `the couple` `, with children` `the kids` `, health` `health` MEANS
    `IL-07 household in a month` WITH
        `the year of the month`                                                          IS `the year`
        `the month of the year`                                                          IS `the month`
        `the earner`                                                                     IS `who earns`
        `the couple, if the earner has a spouse`                                         IS `the couple`
        `the children of the household`                                                  IS `the kids`
        `the health insurance contribution the caller says is deducted for the month`    IS `health`

§§ `The households`

-- H1. A single man, no children, 10,000 a month; March 2026.
-- health: 7,703 x 3.23% + 2,297 x 5.17% = 248.8069 + 118.7549 = 367.5618
`H1` MEANS `test: in` 2026 `month` 3 `, a household of` (`test: an earner` "Amir" `, female:` FALSE `, born` (YMD 1985 4 1) `, paid` 10000) `, married:` NOTHING `, with children` EMPTY `, health` 367.5618

-- H2. A single woman, no children, 10,000 a month; March 2026.
`H2` MEANS `test: in` 2026 `month` 3 `, a household of` (`test: an earner` "Galit" `, female:` TRUE `, born` (YMD 1988 9 15) `, paid` 10000) `, married:` NOTHING `, with children` EMPTY `, health` 367.5618

-- H3. A father, the registered spouse, who claims a separate calculation under
-- s 66(c)(1A); his wife is a housewife; two children, aged 3 and 7 in 2026;
-- 15,000 a month; June 2026.
-- health: 248.8069 + 7,297 x 5.17% (377.2549) = 626.0618
`H3 children` MEANS LIST `test: a child` "Dana" `, born` (YMD 2023 8 20), `test: a child` "Eli" `, born` (YMD 2019 3 10)
`H3` MEANS `test: in` 2026 `month` 6 `, a household of` (`test: an earner` "Avi" `, female:` FALSE `, born` (YMD 1985 4 1) `, paid` 15000) `, married:` (JUST (`test: married to` (`test: a housewife named` "Batya") `, the earner registered:` TRUE `, the earner claims a separate calculation:` TRUE)) `, with children` `H3 children` `, health` 626.0618

