§§ `What the capstone declines, and why`

-- H11: no separate calculation, so s 65 (not encoded) governs: the tax and the
-- net are declined; the deduction and the allowance are not.
-- CHANGED IN 0.2.0 (two values): ITO s 65 is encoded by row IL-08 (source line
-- 2448): the couple's income, 180,000, is charged in the name of the registered
-- spouse, the father; his credits are his own ss 34 and 36 (2.25 points), with
-- no children's points outside a separate calculation (NOTES.md fork K12). Tax
-- 25,392 - 6,534 = 18,858; net 15,000 - 1,571.5 - 420.8811 - 626.0618 + 392 =
-- 12,773.5571. Were: REFUSED BECAUSE "no separate calculation governs the
-- earner's tax, so the couple is assessed under section 65 of the Income Tax
-- Ordinance, which is not encoded".
#ASSERT `IL-07: the income tax for the tax year, in` `H11` EQUALS 18858
-- CHANGED BY THE SCHEDULE J RULING: national insurance 590.9012 (was 420.8811); net
-- 15,000 - 1,571.5 - 590.9012 - 626.0618 + 392 = 12,603.537 (was 12,773.5571, itself
-- new in 0.2.0).
#ASSERT `IL-07: the net income of the household for the month, in` `H11` EQUALS 12603.537
#ASSERT `IL-07: the national insurance contributions deducted from the salary for the month, in` `H11` EQUALS 590.9012
#ASSERT `IL-07: the child allowance for the month, in` `H11` EQUALS 392

-- H12: a single parent's children's points are s 40(b) (not encoded); the
-- allowance is the father's: 173 + 219.
-- CHANGED IN 0.2.0 (two values, the words of the refusal): ITO s 40(b) is
-- encoded by row IL-08 (source lines 1633-1645), and reads facts this household
-- record does not give (a single-parent family, living apart, the children's
-- other parent); with them the tax is 0 (il07-tests-il08.l4, N7). Were: BECAUSE
-- "the credit points for the children of a parent without a spouse are given by
-- section 40(b) of the Income Tax Ordinance, which is not encoded".
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-07: the income tax for the tax year, in` `H12` BECAUSE "the earner has no spouse and has children; section 40(b) gives their credit points, and the household does not give the single-parent facts it reads"
#ASSERT `IL-07: the child allowance for the month, in` `H12` EQUALS 392
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-07: the household's month, in` `H12` BECAUSE "the earner has no spouse and has children; section 40(b) gives their credit points, and the household does not give the single-parent facts it reads"

-- H13, H14: months of 2025 and 2027.
-- CHANGED IN 0.2.0 (three values, the words of the refusal): version 0.2.0
-- composes eight rows, not six (row IL-08's two halves answer tax years from
-- 2024, months from May 2015 and contribution periods from January 2026, so
-- 2026 is still the one period all answer). Were: BECAUSE "IL-07 answers months
-- of 2026 only, the one period all six composed rows answer".
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-07: the net income of the household for the month, in` `H13` BECAUSE "IL-07 answers months of 2026 only, the one period all its composed rows answer"
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-07: the net income of the household for the month, in` `H14` BECAUSE "IL-07 answers months of 2026 only, the one period all its composed rows answer"
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-07: the household's month, in` `H14` BECAUSE "IL-07 answers months of 2026 only, the one period all its composed rows answer"
-- ... and why: in 2025, IL-03's s 121, IL-04's s 334 and IL-05's s 348 decline,
-- while IL-02 and IL-06 answer.
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-03: the tax under section 121 on the earner's salary, in` `H13` BECAUSE "section 121 as it stood before tax year 2026 is not in the deposited text"
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-04: the reduced collection threshold for a month in` 2025 BECAUSE "section 334(a) as it stood before 1 January 2026 is not in the deposited text"
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-05: the income on which the earner's contributions are computed, in` `H13` BECAUSE "this row answers contribution periods from January 2026 only"
#ASSERT (`IL-02: the credit points section 66(c) gives the earner, in` `H3 in 2025` `married as` (`the couple of` `H3 in 2025`))'s `IL-02's points for children, by section 66(c)(4) to (6)` EQUALS 5.5
#ASSERT `IL-06: the household's child allowance for the month, in` `H3 in 2025` `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` FALSE EQUALS 383
-- ... in 2027, IL-03's s 121 answers, but IL-04, IL-05, IL-06 and this row's
-- s 121B figure decline.
#ASSERT `IL-03: the tax under section 121 on the earner's salary, in` `H3 in 2027` EQUALS 25392
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-04: the reduced collection threshold for a month in` 2027 BECAUSE "the reduced collection threshold for 2027 or 2028 had not been published when this encoding was made"
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-05: the income on which the earner's contributions are computed, in` `H3 in 2027` BECAUSE "the figures Schedule K reads for 2027 and later had not been published when this encoding was made"
#ASSERT REFUSED `IL-06: the household's child allowance for the month, in` `H3 in 2027` `, the earner's income chargeable to additional tax:` FALSE BECAUSE "the basic amounts for the child allowance from 1 January 2027 had not been published when this model's sources were fetched"

-- H15: the year's tax is not apportioned unless the salary is the same each month.
